From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:20:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Add support for SM6450
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the resources of the SM6450 camera subsystem: four CSIPHYs, and
three TFE 640 with a CSID each, which drive the RDI paths through the
existing CSID 340 and VFE 340 code.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c |   2 +
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c     | 217 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 219 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 20e0d6604..2d3d737c0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -341,6 +341,7 @@ static u32 vfe_src_pad_code(struct vfe_line *line, u32 sink_code,
 		break;
 	case CAMSS_660:
 	case CAMSS_2290:
+	case CAMSS_6450:
 	case CAMSS_7280:
 	case CAMSS_8x96:
 	case CAMSS_8250:
@@ -1989,6 +1990,7 @@ static int vfe_bpl_align(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 	int ret = 8;
 
 	switch (vfe->camss->res->version) {
+	case CAMSS_6450:
 	case CAMSS_7280:
 	case CAMSS_8250:
 	case CAMSS_8280XP:
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
